{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775378145-r5gLte8HOUzehrpfkDO9","role":"assistant","created":1775378172,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the data I need. Let me collect the on-budget and off-budget receipts for fiscal years 1991-2010.\n\nFrom the bulletins:\n- 1996 bulletin (page 12): has data for 1991-1995\n- 2001 bulletin (page 16): has data for 1996-2000 and some 2001 data\n- 2006 bulletin (page 19): has data for 2001-2005\n- 2011 bulletin (page 20): has data for 2006-2010\n\nLet me extract the data:\n\nFrom 1996 bulletin (page 12):\n- 1991: On-budget = 760,375, Off-budget = 293,885\n- 1992: On-budget = 789,266, Off-budget = 302,426\n- 1993: On-budget = 841,241, Off-budget = 311,934\n- 1994: On-budget = 922,161, Off-budget = 335,026\n- 1995: On-budget = 999,496, Off-budget = 351,080\n\nFrom 2001 bulletin (page 16):\n- 1996: On-budget = 1,085,271, Off-budget = 367,492\n- 1997: On-budget = 1,186,987, Off-budget = 391,989\n- 1998: On-budget = 1,305,621, Off-budget = 415,800\n- 1999: On-budget = 1,382,834, Off-budget = 444,468\n- 2000: On-budget = 1,544,455, Off-budget = 480,583\n\nFrom 2006 bulletin (page 19):\n\n\n- 2001: On-budget = 1,483,525, Off-budget = 507,519\n- 2002: On-budget = 1,337,730, Off-budget = 515,321\n- 2003: On-budget = 1,258,265, Off-budget = 523,842\n- 2004: On-budget = 1,345,040, Off-budget = 534,744\n- 2005: On-budget = 1,575,874, Off-budget = 577,475\n\nFrom 2011 bulletin (page 20):\n- 2006: On-budget = 1,797\n\nI need to continue extracting the 2006 data from the 2011 bulletin. Looking at the 2006 data (page 19), I see the on-budget receipts total 1,797,946 (millions), with off-budget receipts of 608,382 (millions). This means the total receipts for 2006 equal 2,406,328 (millions), combining both on-budget and off-budget figures.\n\nThe 2007 data from the 2011 bulletin (page 20) shows on-budget receipts at 1,932,359 and off-budget at 635,088, totaling 2,567,447. For 2008, on-budget reaches 1,865,279 with off-budget at 658,045, bringing the total to 2,523,324.\n\n2009 appears to be a downturn year, with on-budget dropping to 1,450,355 while off-budget stays relatively stable at 654,010, for a total of 2,104,365. The 2010 data shows on-budget at 1,530,058 and off-budget at 631,688, totaling 2,161,745.\n\nNow I need to calculate R-squared, which requires determining the correlation coefficient between on-budget and off-budget receipts across these years.\n\nI'll write a Python script to compute this: First, I'll extract the paired data for each year from 1991-2010, then calculate the correlation coefficient r, and finally square it to get R².\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_755accabf7b345069c0f8891","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Data for fiscal years 1991-2010 (in millions of dollars)\n# From Treasury Bulletins: 1996-09 (page 12), 2001-09 (page 16), 2006-09 (page 19), 2011-09 (page 20)\n\n# Year: (On-budget receipts, Off-budget receipts)\ndata = {\n    1991: (760375, 293885),\n    1992: (789266, 302426),\n    1993: (841241, 311934),\n    1994: (922161, 335026),\n    1995: (999496, 351080),\n    1996: (1085271, 367492),\n    1997: (1186987, 391989),\n    1998: (1305621, 415800),\n    1999: (1382834, 444468),\n    2000: (1544455, 480583),\n    2001: (1483525, 507519),\n    2002: (1337730, 515321),\n    2003: (1258265, 523842),\n    2004: (1345040, 534744),\n    2005: (1575874, 577475),\n    2006: (1797946, 608382),\n    2007: (1932359, 635088),\n    2008: (1865279, 658045),\n    2009: (1450355, 654010),\n    2010: (1530058, 631688),\n}\n\n# Extract x (on-budget) and y (off-budget)\nyears = sorted(data.keys())\nx = np.array([data[y][0] for y in years])\ny = np.array([data[y][1] for y in years])\n\nprint(\"Fiscal Year | On-Budget (millions) | Off-Budget (millions)\")\nprint(\"-\" * 55)\nfor year in years:\n    print(f\"{year} | {data[year][0]:,} | {data[year][1]:,}\")\n\n# Calculate R-squared\n# Using the formula: R² = (correlation coefficient)²\n# correlation = covariance(x, y) / (std(x) * std(y))\n\nmean_x = np.mean(x)\nmean_y = np.mean(y)\n\n# Calculate covariance\ncov_xy = np.mean((x - mean_x) * (y - mean_y))\n\n# Calculate standard deviations\nstd_x = np.std(x, ddof=0)  # population std\nstd_y = np.std(y, ddof=0)  # population std\n\n# Calculate correlation coefficient\nr = cov_xy / (std_x * std_y)\n\n# Calculate R-squared\nr_squared = r ** 2\n\nprint(f\"\\nMean of on-budget: {mean_x:,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Mean of off-budget: {mean_y:,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Correlation coefficient (r): {r:.10f}\")\nprint(f\"R-squared: {r_squared:.10f}\")\nprint(f\"R-squared (rounded to 4 decimals): {round(r_squared, 4)}\")\n\n# Alternative verification using sklearn\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n\nX = x.reshape(-1, 1)\nmodel = LinearRegression()\nmodel.fit(X, y)\ny_pred = model.predict(X)\nss_res = np.sum((y - y_pred) ** 2)\nss_tot = np.sum((y - mean_y) ** 2)\nr_squared_alt = 1 - (ss_res / ss_tot)\nprint(f\"\\nVerification using sklearn R²: {r_squared_alt:.10f}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
